Title: Link winwrap into the standalone node.exe for Windows XP
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

Only reached when building Node on its own. Electron compiles the same libuv,
V8 and src/ through GN and never reads node.gyp, so this is inert there -- the
same arrangement as 04-node-version-check-winxp.patch.

Two settings, both on the node executable rather than on node_lib or on every
target in the tree.

The dependency and /INCLUDE: belong at the final link because that is where
the __imp_<name> slots are resolved, and it is the link kernel32.lib is also
on. Without the anchor the redirect table is an archive member nothing
references: kernel32 satisfies every slot first, the member is never
extracted, and the build succeeds while redirecting nothing. winwrap.gyp has
the long version, including why /WHOLEARCHIVE is not the answer.

Not applied to cctest or the embedtests: those run on the build machine, and
giving them the anchor without the library is LNK2001.

MinimumRequiredVersion is the other half. winwrap supplies the imports XP
lacks; the subsystem version is what lets XP's loader accept the binary at
all. 5.01 and 5.02 are as low as the linker goes for each machine.

winwrap itself is fetched into deps/winwrap by build_node.sh, and the define
its .asm forwarders guard on needs 12-gyp-masm-settings.patch to reach ml.

Note for anyone editing this: the OS=="win" entry is merged into the node
target's existing 'conditions' list, not given a 'conditions' key of its own.
A .gyp file is a Python literal, so two keys of the same name do not merge --
the last silently wins and the first is discarded. The first version of this
patch did exactly that, and the result parsed cleanly, generated cleanly, and
produced a node.exe with /INCLUDE:_winwrap_static_redirects on the link line
and no winwrap anywhere in the build. The half of the patch that landed in
msvs_settings survived; the half that added a second 'conditions' key did not.
ast.literal_eval cannot catch this, because duplicate keys are legal Python.

diff --git a/node.gyp b/node.gyp
--- a/node.gyp
+++ b/node.gyp
@@ -594,6 +594,31 @@
 
       'msvs_settings': {
         'VCLinkerTool': {
+          'conditions': [
+            # The subsystem version is the other half of running on XP:
+            # winwrap supplies the imports, this is what lets XP's loader
+            # accept the binary at all. 5.01 for Win32 and 5.02 for x64,
+            # as low as the linker goes for each machine.
+            #
+            # /INCLUDE: names winwrap's anchor, forcing the redirect table
+            # into the link. Without it the table is an archive member
+            # nothing references: kernel32.lib is on this link line too, so
+            # it resolves every __imp_<name> first and the member is never
+            # extracted -- a clean build that redirects nothing. The symbol
+            # takes the usual decoration, hence the underscore on x86.
+            ['target_arch=="ia32"', {
+              'MinimumRequiredVersion': '5.01',
+              'AdditionalOptions': [
+                '/INCLUDE:_winwrap_static_redirects',
+              ],
+            }],
+            ['target_arch=="x64"', {
+              'MinimumRequiredVersion': '5.02',
+              'AdditionalOptions': [
+                '/INCLUDE:winwrap_static_redirects',
+              ],
+            }],
+          ],
           'GenerateMapFile': 'true', # /MAP
           'MapExports': 'true', # /MAPINFO:EXPORTS
           'RandomizedBaseAddress': 2, # enable ASLR
@@ -613,6 +638,23 @@
       'msvs_disabled_warnings!': [4244],
 
       'conditions': [
+        # winwrap supplies the Win32 functions XP does not export, by defining
+        # the __imp_<name> slots the call sites load through. It belongs on the
+        # executable rather than on node_lib: the slots are resolved at the final
+        # link, and that is the link kernel32.lib is also on.
+        #
+        # Merged into this list rather than given a 'conditions' key of its own.
+        # A .gyp file is a Python literal, so a second key of the same name does
+        # not merge -- the last one silently wins and the first is discarded,
+        # which parses perfectly and builds a node.exe with no winwrap in it.
+        #
+        # Only this target. cctest and the embedtests run on the build machine,
+        # and giving them the /INCLUDE: below without the library is LNK2001.
+        [ 'OS=="win"', {
+          'dependencies': [
+            'deps/winwrap/winwrap.gyp:winwrap',
+          ],
+        }],
         [ 'node_shared_hdr_histogram=="false"', {
           'dependencies': [
             'deps/histogram/histogram.gyp:histogram',
